# ===========================================================================
# openclaw-file-chat — what stays OUT of the repository
# ===========================================================================

# --- Dependencies ----------------------------------------------------------
# Installed per checkout by whoever works on the plugin. Never commit.
#
# The leading "/" is deliberate: it anchors the rule to the repository root.
# A bare `node_modules/` would also match `.smoke/node_modules/`, which holds
# the hand-written SDK stubs the smoke test needs in order to resolve bare
# `openclaw/plugin-sdk/*` imports. Those stubs MUST stay committed.
/node_modules/

# --- Smoke-test scratch output --------------------------------------------
# Both are deleted and regenerated by `npm run smoke` on every run:
#   .smoke/dist     -> a fresh copy of ../dist, so the test never loads a stale build
#   .smoke/workspace -> the fake filesRoot the test writes fixtures into
#
# Keep these committed instead:
#   .smoke/run.mjs
#   .smoke/node_modules/openclaw/**   (test stubs, NOT a real dependency)
.smoke/dist/
.smoke/workspace/

# --- Packed artifacts ------------------------------------------------------
*.tgz
*.tar.gz

# --- Secrets / local overrides --------------------------------------------
# The plugin's apiKey is configured in openclaw.json on the target host.
# Never let a real key reach the repository.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Local runtime data ----------------------------------------------------
# Default filesRoot is ~/.openclaw/file-chat/files, i.e. outside the repo, so
# nothing lands here normally. Uncomment if you point filesRoot inside the repo.
# /files/

# --- Logs and caches -------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
*.tsbuildinfo
.cache/
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# --- OS clutter ------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Editor clutter --------------------------------------------------------
# Shared settings are allowed through; personal/global ones are not.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ===========================================================================
# DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED — read before "tidying up" this file
# ===========================================================================
#
#   dist/               The built JavaScript is committed ON PURPOSE.
#   package-lock.json   Pinned dev toolchain (typescript, @types/node).
#
# Why dist/ is committed:
#   OpenClaw git installs run exactly this, on the target machine:
#
#       npm install --omit=dev --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund
#                                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
#   `--ignore-scripts` means `npm run build` NEVER runs there, and the plugin
#   is loaded from `openclaw.runtimeExtensions` -> ./dist/index.js. A missing
#   or stale dist/ therefore means the plugin simply fails to load.
#
#   So: after editing any .ts file, run `npm run build` and commit the changed
#   dist/ output in the SAME commit as the source change.
